# tools/ales_tube_witness.rish — the asymmetric tube drive: a different ceiling per sign, the DRIVE family's first clip that is not odd (ALES82).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES82.
# Design read: active-designing/20260814-212318_fill-ales82-lotus-tube-drive.md
# Stands on: lotus/drive.rye (ALES78 — the pre-gain, the gain faults, and the ceiling law, reused with one ceiling per sign); lotus/timeline.rye
# (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_min/max, the one true saturate). A keeper who wants an asymmetric overdrive composes this with ALES79 over the same span.
#
# lotus/tube.rye splits ALES78's single ceiling into ceil_pos for the positive half and ceil_neg for the negative, pinning each half to its own. When
# ceil_pos == ceil_neg the two branches collapse into ALES78's hard clip byte-for-byte — the family recognition. When they differ the map is NOT odd:
# tube(1000) = ceil_pos while tube(−1000) = −ceil_neg, a symmetric input driven to an asymmetric output — a DC offset and a full set of EVEN
# harmonics, the tube's honest even-harmonic signature (the sibling of ALES81's not-odd map — the bit-crush floors downward, the tube clips
# unevenly). The selftest proves it: equal ceilings reproduce ALES78's real hard drive byte-for-byte; a hand-computed asymmetric clip matches exactly
# (ceil_pos 1500, ceil_neg 800, ×2: 500→1000, 1000→1500, −300→−600, −600→−800, −100→−200); the map is not odd (tube(1000)=1500, tube(−1000)=−800);
# each half stays under its own ceiling and the sign is held under a heavy ×8 drive; a symmetric-ceiling drive stays ODD; the span discipline holds; a
# zero den / below-unity gain / oversized numerator refuses BadGain, either ceiling zero or over-rail BadCeiling, a span past the end BadRange, each
# leaving the clip untouched. The asymmetric pin lands every output in [−ceil_neg, ceil_pos] BEFORE the write, so the clip is the pin and the saturate
# a documented no-op. Purely local — one multiply, one divide, one sign-aware pin per sample; no delay line, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no
# funds, no real device, no real sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_tube_witness.rish

say "ales-tube: Language EN — the hard clip (ALES78), the overdrive (ALES79), and the wavefolder (ALES80) all shape the sample's MAGNITUDE and carry its SIGN — they are ODD functions, so a symmetric input drives to a symmetric output and only ODD harmonics arise. The tube drive breaks that symmetry on purpose: it pins the positive half of the wave at one ceiling and the negative half at another. A real vacuum-tube stage clips harder on one polarity than the other, and that uneven clipping is exactly where a tube's warm EVEN-order harmonics are born — the second harmonic a symmetric transistor clip never makes."
say "ales-tube: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively as a recognition: ONE CEILING PER SIGN IS THE PLAINEST ASYMMETRY THERE IS, and a hard clip is the tube drive whose two ceilings are EQUAL. When they differ the uneven rail is the tube's honest even-harmonic signature, not a flaw to correct — the sibling of ALES81's not-odd map, where the bit-crush floors downward and the tube clips unevenly, and neither dresses itself in a symmetry it does not have."
say "ales-tube: Lens TAME — one mono clip of i16 PCM driven in place over a span; boosted = divTrunc(x·num, den) (ALES78's pre-gain, verbatim, in i64 under max_drive_num), then y = pin(boosted, +ceil_pos, −ceil_neg), the asymmetric pin landing every output in [−ceil_neg, ceil_pos] ⊆ [sample_min, sample_max] BEFORE the write, the saturate a documented no-op; the map is MEMORYLESS (every output depends only on its own input); equal ceilings reproduce ALES78's hard clip byte-for-byte, unequal ceilings make the map not odd; a zero den / below-unity gain / oversized numerator refuses BadGain, either ceiling outside [1, sample_max] BadCeiling, a span outside the samples BadRange, each before any write, the clip untouched on refusal; siloed to lotus/, the gain a rational num/den and the two ceilings magnitudes in sample units, no delay line, no anti-aliasing, no snapshot, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/tube"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/tube.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-tube: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/tube.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-tube: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-tube: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-tube' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-tube: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-tube line"
